{"text": "Science is the study of things that can be observed or measured in our material reality. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> We have built the modern world on a set of processes that we call the scientific method that advance our understanding of the nature of that reality. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Metaphysics, on the other hand, is the study of the things that lie outside of that material reality, such as the nature of the mind, consciousness, being, causality, and, well, pretty much everything we wonder about but do not have a scientific way to investigate. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The line between the two is fuzzy, and it shifts as science solves old mysteries and uncovers new ones. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But it would be a mistake to say that scientific truths are the only ones we can ever know for certain. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Rather, they are the only ones we can prove, a very different thing. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In point of fact, the vast majority of what you know cannot be scientifically proven. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The old reporters adage, If your mother says she loves you, check it out, is funny because you cannot check it out, but you can obviously know it to be true.", "alignment": {"characters": ["S", "c", "i", "e", "n", "c", "e", " ", "i", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "t", "u", "d", "y", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "i", "n", "g", "s", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "c", "a", "n", " ", "b", "e", " ", "o", "b", "s", "e", "r", "v", "e", "d", " ", "o", "r", " ", "m", "e", "a", "s", "u", "r", "e", "d", " ", "i", "n", " ", "o", "u", "r", " ", "m", "a", "t", "e", "r", "i", "a", "l", " ", "r", "e", "a", "l", "i", "t", "y", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "W", "e", " ", "h", "a", "v", "e", " ", "b", "u", "i", "l", "t", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "m", "o", "d", "e", "r", "n", " ", "w", "o", "r", "l", "d", " ", "o", "n", " ", "a", " ", "s", "e", "t", " ", "o", "f"